and, where the scope is resolved to a directory:

+    if scope == "desired":
+        return specs_dir / "desired_program_model"

THE ALTERNATIVE THE FINDING ALSO OFFERED, and which is cheaper: stop scaffolding
tests into the desired tree and say plainly in the scaffold README that the
desired tree carries no executable conformance. Either resolves the finding;
what must not survive is the current state, where the suite exists, is copied
forward, and silently proves nothing. SI-05 takes no position on which — that is
the owner's call, and it is recorded here rather than decided in a ticket that
does not own the file.

Expected first result if the scope is added: SF-202 records that the binding
reconciliation test in that tree had been asserting "fourteen command actions"
against a fifteen-action module since AC-01 closed, so the first `--scope
desired` run is expected to FAIL, and that failure is the finding being true.
